1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:04,089
Everyone who tells this story

2
00:00:04,530 --> 00:00:06,910
will tell you why it was never solved.

3
00:00:07,820 --> 00:00:09,800
A crowd walked through the rooms.

4
00:00:10,509 --> 00:00:11,650
The evidence was lost.

5
00:00:12,109 --> 00:00:13,390
And that is partly true.

6
00:00:14,089 --> 00:00:16,429
But here is what the paperwork shows.

7
00:00:17,150 --> 00:00:19,710
This case did not run out of evidence.

8
00:00:20,449 --> 00:00:21,490
For nineteen years

9
00:00:22,390 --> 00:00:23,320
it kept getting more.

10
00:00:24,019 --> 00:00:24,620
A closet.

11
00:00:25,280 --> 00:00:28,980
A photograph, said to come from inside a child's eye.

12
00:00:29,710 --> 00:00:31,970
A sound that turned into a man.

13
00:00:32,649 --> 00:00:33,780
A signed confession.

14
00:00:34,469 --> 00:00:35,210
A fingerprint.

15
00:00:45,488 --> 00:00:48,508
On the morning of June tenth, nineteen twelve,

16
00:00:49,218 --> 00:00:51,368
a mother in southwest Iowa

17
00:00:52,058 --> 00:00:53,588
telephoned a neighbor's house.

18
00:00:54,308 --> 00:00:56,708
Her husband told the coroner about it.

19
00:00:57,538 --> 00:00:58,608
My wife did, yes.

20
00:00:59,368 --> 00:01:00,798
He could not say what time.

21
00:01:01,478 --> 00:01:02,528
She tried, he said,

22
00:01:03,228 --> 00:01:04,868
about three different times.

23
00:01:05,638 --> 00:01:07,948
Her two daughters had stayed the night there.

24
00:01:08,538 --> 00:01:09,838
She expected them back.

25
00:01:11,238 --> 00:01:12,838
That house was locked.

26
00:01:12,998 --> 00:01:13,598
The blinds were down.

27
00:01:14,228 --> 00:01:17,778
I can't tell you who killed eight people in Villisca.

28
00:01:18,528 --> 00:01:19,198
No one can.

29
00:01:19,878 --> 00:01:22,038
What I can give you is an inventory.

30
00:01:22,458 --> 00:01:23,318
What was in that house.

31
00:01:24,078 --> 00:01:26,378
And what was carried in afterward.

32
00:01:27,081 --> 00:01:28,801
The first entry is the people.

33
00:01:29,371 --> 00:01:30,661
Joe Moore was forty-three.

34
00:01:31,211 --> 00:01:32,561
He sold farm implements.

35
00:01:33,151 --> 00:01:34,651
Sarah Moore was thirty-nine,

36
00:01:35,201 --> 00:01:37,841
and she helped run the Children's Day program

37
00:01:38,461 --> 00:01:39,861
at the Presbyterian church.

38
00:01:40,441 --> 00:01:41,201
Herman was eleven.

39
00:01:41,771 --> 00:01:42,681
That Sunday night,

40
00:01:43,251 --> 00:01:45,361
he spoke a piece

41
00:01:46,261 --> 00:01:47,561
about God watching over the sparrows.

42
00:01:48,131 --> 00:01:49,541
Katherine was ten.

43
00:01:50,081 --> 00:01:50,911
Boyd was seven.

44
00:01:51,481 --> 00:01:52,311
Paul was five.

45
00:01:52,891 --> 00:01:55,551
Lena Stillinger took part in the program too.

46
00:01:56,461 --> 00:01:58,761
Her sister Ina was with her.

47
00:01:59,361 --> 00:02:01,601
The records disagree about their ages.

48
00:02:02,181 --> 00:02:04,351
Lena was eleven or twelve.

49
00:02:04,911 --> 00:02:05,511
Ina was eight or nine,

50
00:02:05,821 --> 00:02:08,781
and one trial report says six.

51
00:02:09,081 --> 00:02:09,681
At six o'clock that evening,

52
00:02:10,081 --> 00:02:13,741
according to their older sister Blanche,

53
00:02:14,321 --> 00:02:16,891
Joe Moore telephoned the Stillinger home.

54
00:02:17,461 --> 00:02:20,941
He did not want the girls walking back in the dark.

55
00:02:21,541 --> 00:02:22,661
Could they stay with his family?

56
00:02:23,221 --> 00:02:24,721
Blanche said she thought that would be all right.

57
00:02:25,351 --> 00:02:29,351
The pastor testified the program ended about nine fifteen.

58
00:02:29,891 --> 00:02:31,721
Nobody who saw what came next

59
00:02:32,421 --> 00:02:34,091
ever gave an account that held.

60
00:02:34,751 --> 00:02:35,981
So I won't give you one.

61
00:02:36,623 --> 00:02:37,223
Monday morning.

62
00:02:37,893 --> 00:02:39,773
A neighbor, Mary Peckham,

63
00:02:40,483 --> 00:02:42,803
noticed how still the house was.

64
00:02:43,523 --> 00:02:44,503
She tried the doors.

65
00:02:45,223 --> 00:02:47,613
Joe's brother Ross came with a key.

66
00:02:48,343 --> 00:02:50,283
He opened the door to the room off the parlor.

67
00:02:50,993 --> 00:02:51,713
He told the coroner

68
00:02:52,433 --> 00:02:55,163
he did not wait long enough to see anything else.

69
00:02:55,893 --> 00:02:59,143
The town marshal, Hank Horton, went through every room.

70
00:02:59,823 --> 00:03:01,263
And then he did something

71
00:03:01,963 --> 00:03:03,913
almost nobody retells.

72
00:03:04,773 --> 00:03:06,483
According to the Moore store clerk,

73
00:03:07,263 --> 00:03:08,483
he locked the house

74
00:03:09,213 --> 00:03:11,093
and left the keys with the neighbor.

75
00:03:11,793 --> 00:03:12,393
Remember that.

76
00:03:12,793 --> 00:03:13,643
A locked house.

77
00:03:14,383 --> 00:03:16,543
A woman next door, holding the key.

78
00:03:17,243 --> 00:03:19,343
It is the last moment anyone could say

79
00:03:20,033 --> 00:03:20,983
who had been inside.

80
00:03:21,763 --> 00:03:22,783
When the doctors went in,

81
00:03:23,463 --> 00:03:24,563
every face was covered.

82
00:03:25,363 --> 00:03:27,423
Dr. Williams climbed the stairs

83
00:03:28,133 --> 00:03:29,883
to the room on the south side.

84
00:03:30,693 --> 00:03:32,563
A small boy, on his stomach.

85
00:03:33,353 --> 00:03:34,363
A gauze undershirt

86
00:03:35,133 --> 00:03:36,743
laid over the top of his head.

87
00:03:37,473 --> 00:03:41,573
Dr. Williams told the inquest what he did next.

88
00:03:42,483 --> 00:03:43,423
I lifted that off

89
00:03:44,323 --> 00:03:45,063
lifted it off

90
00:03:45,963 --> 00:03:47,183
to see which one it was.

91
00:03:52,914 --> 00:03:54,365
So here is the first inventory.

92
00:03:54,814 --> 00:03:57,844
An ax, near the bed where Lena and Ina were found.

93
00:03:58,395 --> 00:04:00,974
A piece of bacon, wrapped in a flour sack,

94
00:04:01,525 --> 00:04:02,435
at the head of that bed.

95
00:04:02,935 --> 00:04:05,884
A lamp on the floor, at the foot of the parents' bed.

96
00:04:06,335 --> 00:04:08,544
The marshal moved it out of the way.

97
00:04:08,985 --> 00:04:11,335
Skirts and aprons hung over the windows.

98
00:04:11,775 --> 00:04:12,995
Marks in the ceiling.

99
00:04:13,395 --> 00:04:15,275
Dr. Williams found no footprints.

100
00:04:15,745 --> 00:04:16,714
Five years later,

101
00:04:17,154 --> 00:04:18,274
the coroner testified

102
00:04:18,725 --> 00:04:21,024
there were no finger marks on the ax handle.

103
00:04:21,475 --> 00:04:22,814
Then the house was opened again.

104
00:04:23,274 --> 00:04:25,824
The National Guard came to hold the line.

105
00:04:26,235 --> 00:04:28,685
One account says ten thirty.

106
00:04:29,115 --> 00:04:30,215
Another says noon.

107
00:04:30,644 --> 00:04:33,754
How many people went in before that, I can't tell you.

108
00:04:34,194 --> 00:04:37,074
Later accounts say one hundred.

109
00:04:37,495 --> 00:04:38,555
Others say hundreds.

110
00:04:39,014 --> 00:04:40,855
I have not found a count from that day.

111
00:04:41,274 --> 00:04:42,375
What the record does show

112
00:04:42,834 --> 00:04:45,444
is a house entered again and again.

113
00:04:45,855 --> 00:04:48,735
Jessie Moore testified she went in that day,

114
00:04:49,175 --> 00:04:51,324
to get family pictures for the press.

115
00:04:51,774 --> 00:04:52,745
Bedding was burned.

116
00:04:53,204 --> 00:04:55,715
The house was cleaned, then repapered.

117
00:04:56,154 --> 00:04:56,754
So yes.

118
00:04:57,165 --> 00:04:57,894
Things were lost.

119
00:04:58,355 --> 00:05:00,465
But loss only explains what disappeared.

120
00:05:01,165 --> 00:05:03,475
It cannot explain what showed up.

121
00:05:04,238 --> 00:05:07,848
Item one arrives five days after the murders.

122
00:05:08,298 --> 00:05:11,298
A newspaper report, datelined Omaha.

123
00:05:11,748 --> 00:05:13,508
A woman named Retta Johnson

124
00:05:13,958 --> 00:05:15,368
has come back from Villisca.

125
00:05:16,278 --> 00:05:18,918
There is a closet, she says,

126
00:05:19,358 --> 00:05:22,588
off the room where the Stillinger girls slept.

127
00:05:23,048 --> 00:05:24,688
Bags of cotton batting inside.

128
00:05:25,188 --> 00:05:27,288
On them, the marks of a man

129
00:05:27,728 --> 00:05:29,308
who had sat and stood there.

130
00:05:29,748 --> 00:05:30,838
And in the girls' bed,

131
00:05:31,288 --> 00:05:32,548
a piece of watch chain.

132
00:05:32,978 --> 00:05:34,058
Now follow the closet.

133
00:05:34,518 --> 00:05:36,648
By the trial, five years on,

134
00:05:37,088 --> 00:05:40,268
the list of exhibits names a closet upstairs.

135
00:05:40,728 --> 00:05:45,048
A public comment posted under historian Edgar Epperly's name

136
00:05:45,488 --> 00:05:49,528
traces a version of the story to a Kansas City reporter,

137
00:05:49,958 --> 00:05:52,548
with cigarettes, and a heel print in the dust.

138
00:05:53,068 --> 00:05:55,548
It says an undertaker checked,

139
00:05:56,018 --> 00:05:58,678
and the box of cotton sat on two suit boxes

140
00:05:59,238 --> 00:06:01,128
that had not been crushed.

141
00:06:01,598 --> 00:06:04,368
Today, you will hear it was the attic.

142
00:06:04,828 --> 00:06:07,168
Now follow the chain.

143
00:06:07,808 --> 00:06:09,628
A watch chain, in a bed, in June.

144
00:06:10,058 --> 00:06:10,908
By the trial,

145
00:06:11,358 --> 00:06:13,178
a piece of key chain,

146
00:06:13,598 --> 00:06:16,428
and Joe Moore's watch, on the floor.

147
00:06:16,888 --> 00:06:18,548
The containers stayed the same.

148
00:06:19,238 --> 00:06:21,548
What was inside them kept changing.

149
00:06:22,216 --> 00:06:23,446
August, nineteen twelve.

150
00:06:24,166 --> 00:06:27,946
A man from Villisca tells people in Council Bluffs

151
00:06:28,666 --> 00:06:34,106
that detectives have a photograph of the killer.

152
00:06:34,806 --> 00:06:35,406
They got it, he says,

153
00:06:35,866 --> 00:06:40,016
from the retina of one of the Stillinger sisters.

154
00:06:40,146 --> 00:06:43,946
I have found no such photograph in any record.

155
00:06:44,526 --> 00:06:47,866
Her parents were alive to read that.

156
00:06:48,766 --> 00:06:49,786
By the end of that year,

157
00:06:50,496 --> 00:06:55,106
newspapers had reported at least five different men held or arrested.

158
00:06:55,856 --> 00:06:57,146
A brother-in-law.

159
00:06:57,846 --> 00:06:58,506
A man with stained shoes.

160
00:06:58,976 --> 00:07:01,706
A farmhand who wrote about a vision.

161
00:07:02,616 --> 00:07:05,476
A Sioux City porter,

162
00:07:06,186 --> 00:07:09,306
whom the headline identified by his race.

163
00:07:09,996 --> 00:07:10,596
A farmer.

164
00:07:11,136 --> 00:07:13,986
None of them was convicted of anything at Villisca.

165
00:07:14,896 --> 00:07:18,426
The question had stopped being what happened in the house.

166
00:07:19,146 --> 00:07:19,946
It had become

167
00:07:20,736 --> 00:07:22,066
who was going to pay for it.

168
00:07:22,998 --> 00:07:24,418
In nineteen sixteen,

169
00:07:24,828 --> 00:07:27,548
a private detective named James Wilkerson

170
00:07:27,938 --> 00:07:29,078
brought the case a theory.

171
00:07:29,518 --> 00:07:30,958
State senator Frank Jones,

172
00:07:31,408 --> 00:07:34,418
Joe Moore's old employer and business rival,

173
00:07:34,848 --> 00:07:35,618
had hired a killer.

174
00:07:36,048 --> 00:07:38,668
Wilkerson's man was William Mansfield.

175
00:07:39,128 --> 00:07:41,018
A grand jury refused to indict him.

176
00:07:41,458 --> 00:07:44,298
Frank Jones was never charged with anything.

177
00:07:44,658 --> 00:07:46,548
He sued Wilkerson for slander,

178
00:07:46,968 --> 00:07:48,648
asked for sixty thousand dollars,

179
00:07:49,078 --> 00:07:49,828
and lost.

180
00:07:50,268 --> 00:07:51,278
And in that lawsuit,

181
00:07:51,758 --> 00:07:54,408
a witness named Ed Landers took the oath.

182
00:07:54,958 --> 00:07:56,218
You have met Landers already,

183
00:07:56,938 --> 00:07:57,558
in a way.

184
00:07:57,978 --> 00:08:00,318
He was staying a few houses from the Moores.

185
00:08:00,738 --> 00:08:02,438
At the inquest in nineteen twelve,

186
00:08:02,838 --> 00:08:04,938
he described something he heard that Sunday night.

187
00:08:05,438 --> 00:08:06,038
A sound.

188
00:08:06,698 --> 00:08:08,658
Like one boy hooting for another.

189
00:08:09,078 --> 00:08:11,918
The next day, he said, it occurred to him

190
00:08:12,348 --> 00:08:13,798
it might have been a woman moaning.

191
00:08:14,218 --> 00:08:16,318
In the published summary of that testimony,

192
00:08:16,748 --> 00:08:17,838
that is all there is.

193
00:08:18,308 --> 00:08:18,908
Four years later,

194
00:08:19,378 --> 00:08:20,818
under oath,

195
00:08:21,548 --> 00:08:22,788
he said that on that same night

196
00:08:23,208 --> 00:08:25,578
he saw Frank Jones's son, Albert,

197
00:08:25,988 --> 00:08:27,098
go into the Moore home.

198
00:08:27,998 --> 00:08:31,938
Albert Jones was never charged either.

199
00:08:32,368 --> 00:08:33,988
Both men denied any part in it.

200
00:08:34,428 --> 00:08:38,268
The prosecution attacked Landers's account in open court.

201
00:08:38,718 --> 00:08:39,518
A sound

202
00:08:40,418 --> 00:08:41,098
became a man.

203
00:08:46,779 --> 00:08:50,469
In nineteen seventeen, the state found its own document.

204
00:08:51,029 --> 00:08:53,269
The Reverend Lyn George Kelly

205
00:08:53,669 --> 00:08:54,699
was a traveling preacher,

206
00:08:55,129 --> 00:08:56,639
in town for one Sunday.

207
00:08:57,069 --> 00:08:59,869
He was charged with the murder of Lena Stillinger.

208
00:09:00,319 --> 00:09:02,779
He had been charged with mailing obscene letters,

209
00:09:03,229 --> 00:09:06,149
and he had been held in a federal mental hospital.

210
00:09:06,579 --> 00:09:10,149
He caught the five nineteen train that morning.

211
00:09:10,559 --> 00:09:14,029
The train left hours before anyone opened the door.

212
00:09:14,469 --> 00:09:16,769
Witnesses swore he spoke of the murders

213
00:09:17,189 --> 00:09:18,639
before the bodies were found.

214
00:09:19,179 --> 00:09:20,589
They swore it five years later.

215
00:09:21,019 --> 00:09:24,429
A station ticket record backed up the date of one encounter.

216
00:09:24,849 --> 00:09:26,289
It could not record what was said.

217
00:09:26,709 --> 00:09:27,969
Then, Logan jail.

218
00:09:28,389 --> 00:09:29,189
August thirtieth.

219
00:09:29,599 --> 00:09:31,489
A newspaper editor testified

220
00:09:31,979 --> 00:09:34,769
that he was handcuffed and placed in Kelly's cell,

221
00:09:35,189 --> 00:09:36,429
playing an automobile thief.

222
00:09:36,859 --> 00:09:38,569
A sheriff read out accusations.

223
00:09:39,029 --> 00:09:41,749
The editor recalled eighty-seven paragraphs.

224
00:09:42,189 --> 00:09:42,829
Kelly said,

225
00:09:43,249 --> 00:09:43,849
that's a lie.

226
00:09:44,189 --> 00:09:47,519
Early the next morning, a county attorney took down a statement.

227
00:09:48,299 --> 00:09:49,999
Its first lines say it was made

228
00:09:50,429 --> 00:09:52,819
without any promise or threats.

229
00:09:53,359 --> 00:09:56,129
In it, a voice tells Kelly to slay utterly.

230
00:09:56,509 --> 00:09:59,409
He climbs the stairs, thinking they are Jacob's ladder.

231
00:09:59,849 --> 00:10:01,829
He kills the children first, it says.

232
00:10:02,259 --> 00:10:03,129
Then the parents.

233
00:10:03,579 --> 00:10:05,849
No record I have read can tell you

234
00:10:06,549 --> 00:10:08,109
whether that is the order it happened.

235
00:10:08,829 --> 00:10:11,769
The attorney general told the jury

236
00:10:12,299 --> 00:10:13,549
Kelly had been asked fifteen times

237
00:10:13,979 --> 00:10:15,469
whether he killed the parents first.

238
00:10:15,939 --> 00:10:18,119
And fifteen times, he said no.

239
00:10:18,539 --> 00:10:21,899
Twenty-five times, he was told no promise could be made.

240
00:10:22,309 --> 00:10:25,649
Fifty-one times, he was told to tell the truth.

241
00:10:26,109 --> 00:10:27,169
The state counted those.

242
00:10:27,609 --> 00:10:30,069
It offered them as proof that he was free.

243
00:10:30,519 --> 00:10:32,229
At trial, Kelly said

244
00:10:32,649 --> 00:10:35,849
I have no recollection of signing that paper.

245
00:10:36,599 --> 00:10:38,329
The record shows a signature.

246
00:10:39,029 --> 00:10:42,489
It cannot show you what the signature is worth.

247
00:10:43,280 --> 00:10:46,270
There is one more name in the Omaha paper.

248
00:10:47,010 --> 00:10:49,310
A committee was raising money for Kelly's defense.

249
00:10:50,090 --> 00:10:50,950
It held meetings.

250
00:10:51,680 --> 00:10:52,420
It passed the hat.

251
00:10:53,170 --> 00:10:54,490
Its officers are listed.

252
00:10:55,250 --> 00:10:57,140
Remember the man who told the coroner

253
00:10:57,890 --> 00:10:58,960
my wife did, yes.

254
00:10:59,720 --> 00:11:01,640
She phoned about three different times.

255
00:11:02,390 --> 00:11:04,300
The state of Iowa had charged Kelly

256
00:11:05,080 --> 00:11:06,100
with killing his daughter.

257
00:11:07,510 --> 00:11:08,630
And Joseph Stillinger

258
00:11:09,370 --> 00:11:10,620
was the president of the committee

259
00:11:11,380 --> 00:11:12,200
trying to set him free.

260
00:11:17,915 --> 00:11:19,275
The paper does not say why.

261
00:11:19,755 --> 00:11:23,435
The committee said it wanted the guilty man brought to justice.

262
00:11:23,895 --> 00:11:25,605
It did not believe it had him.

263
00:11:26,025 --> 00:11:28,365
The first jury took twenty ballots.

264
00:11:28,805 --> 00:11:31,155
Eleven for acquittal, every time.

265
00:11:31,595 --> 00:11:37,355
One man, W. C. Brown, held for not guilty by reason of insanity.

266
00:11:37,815 --> 00:11:40,995
In November, a second jury acquitted Kelly.

267
00:11:41,465 --> 00:11:43,435
He was found not guilty.

268
00:11:43,855 --> 00:11:44,555
That is the verdict.

269
00:11:45,165 --> 00:11:46,575
There is one last item.

270
00:11:47,025 --> 00:11:48,635
March, nineteen thirty-one.

271
00:11:49,045 --> 00:11:51,195
A man in a Detroit jail,

272
00:11:51,645 --> 00:11:53,305
after five hours with detectives,

273
00:11:53,775 --> 00:11:56,495
confesses to the Villisca murders.

274
00:11:56,995 --> 00:11:57,905
The papers report

275
00:11:58,495 --> 00:12:01,235
that his fingerprints matched prints found at the scene.

276
00:12:01,655 --> 00:12:02,465
Remember the coroner.

277
00:12:02,935 --> 00:12:04,215
No finger marks on the handle.

278
00:12:04,655 --> 00:12:07,245
And this man's confession has a problem.

279
00:12:07,715 --> 00:12:08,805
He says he killed a man,

280
00:12:09,255 --> 00:12:09,855
his wife,

281
00:12:10,335 --> 00:12:12,845
and their four children.

282
00:12:13,265 --> 00:12:13,875
Six people.

283
00:12:14,595 --> 00:12:16,715
Officers said it did not tally.

284
00:12:17,415 --> 00:12:18,815
The last confession in the file

285
00:12:19,715 --> 00:12:21,785
forgot Lena and Ina.

286
00:12:27,508 --> 00:12:29,518
So here is the inventory now.

287
00:12:30,268 --> 00:12:30,888
A house.

288
00:12:31,678 --> 00:12:32,278
An ax.

289
00:12:32,998 --> 00:12:33,868
A few photographs.

290
00:12:34,618 --> 00:12:36,018
Everything else was carried in.

291
00:12:36,778 --> 00:12:39,558
Some of it, by people with something to gain.

292
00:12:39,988 --> 00:12:41,508
Much of it, I think,

293
00:12:42,258 --> 00:12:45,498
by people who could not stand an empty line on the form.

294
00:12:46,238 --> 00:12:48,258
That is what this kind of crime does.

295
00:12:49,028 --> 00:12:52,318
It leaves a space the exact size of a name.

296
00:12:53,068 --> 00:12:54,608
And a town will put anything in it.

297
00:12:55,368 --> 00:12:55,978
A stranger.

298
00:12:56,718 --> 00:12:57,318
A senator.

299
00:12:58,058 --> 00:12:59,538
A preacher who heard voices.

300
00:13:00,308 --> 00:13:03,488
No one has ever been convicted of these murders.

301
00:13:03,958 --> 00:13:05,708
Reverend Kelly was acquitted.

302
00:13:06,158 --> 00:13:08,638
Frank and Albert Jones were never charged.

303
00:13:09,098 --> 00:13:10,358
The one thing in this file

304
00:13:11,098 --> 00:13:13,318
that nobody needed to invent

305
00:13:14,068 --> 00:13:15,188
is a mother,

306
00:13:15,938 --> 00:13:16,928
on a Monday morning,

307
00:13:17,668 --> 00:13:18,558
calling a house.

308
00:13:19,348 --> 00:13:20,988
About three different times.

309
00:13:21,908 --> 00:13:27,258
This film is drawn from court testimony and newspapers of the time.

310
00:13:27,698 --> 00:13:29,248
A report is not proof.

311
00:13:29,698 --> 00:13:34,478
Everyone named here is presumed innocent of these murders.
